  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which builds the island scene. It passes typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser, so I haven't seen a rendered frame and none of the visuals are verified.\n\n- **Island:** A flat-shaded terrain mesh with one normal and one colour per triangle, built from a height function. The shoreline is irregular, and the colours run sand, grass, rock and snow. About 26 low-poly pine trees and 14 rocks sit on it as instanced primitives.\n- **Water:** A 320 m grid with a custom GLSL material. Waves move in the vertex shader, and the fragment shader uses faceted normals, a Fresnel blend with the sky colour, a sun glint, shallow-to-deep colour, and a fade to the horizon colour. It is opaque and has no shoreline foam.\n- **Day/night:** A 20 s cycle, starting at 08:00. Each frame, the sun and moon lights, the hemisphere light, the Preetham sky, the fog colour and the water uniforms are updated from the sun's elevation. The night floor is a moon light of intensity 0.9 plus a hemisphere light of 0.28, so the scene should not go black.\n- **Camera:** It orbits slowly at radius 34 and height 17, set each frame with `app.camera?.setPose`. I didn't confirm that this works on a `camera.perspective` camera.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()` resolves.\n\n",
